dt-bindings: opp: describe the RKNPU OPP table

The NPU OPP table carries two properties the generic operating-points-v2
schema has no place for: a phandle to the NPU GRF, and the table mapping
rail voltage to the memory read margin the driver programs alongside it.
Nothing described them, so a node using them passed dtc and would have
failed dtbs_check.

Give them a compatible of their own, following the same shape as the
other SoC-specific OPP tables, and require the two properties together -
half a configuration leaves the margin at its reset value, which is what
having it at all is meant to prevent. The margin is bounded to the three
bits the register field has, and the table to the eight entries the
driver stores.

Operating points that share a frequency across variants need distinct
node names, so the child pattern allows a second number after the
frequency; opp-supported-hw still selects between them.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/opp-v2-rknpu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/opp-v2-rknpu.yaml
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/opp-v2-rknpu.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/opp/opp-v2-rknpu.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Rockchip RKNPU OPP table
+
+maintainers:
+  - Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>
+
+allOf:
+  - $ref: opp-v2-base.yaml#
+
+description: |
+  The NPU on some Rockchip SoCs carries a memory read-margin setting that has
+  to track the operating voltage. It lives in the NPU GRF and is rewritten as
+  part of each voltage transition, so the table that defines the operating
+  points also describes where the setting is and which value each voltage
+  needs.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: operating-points-v2-rknpu
+
+  rockchip,grf:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      Phandle to the NPU general register file holding the memory read-margin
+      registers.
+
+  rockchip,volt-mem-read-margin:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
+    description:
+      Voltage thresholds and the read margin each requires, highest voltage
+      first. The margin for an operating point is taken from the first entry
+      whose threshold is at or below its voltage.
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 8
+    items:
+      items:
+        - description: voltage threshold in microvolts
+        - description: read margin to program at or above that voltage
+          maximum: 7
+
+patternProperties:
+  '^opp(-[0-9]+){1,2}$':
+    type: object
+    additionalProperties: false
+    description:
+      A trailing second number distinguishes operating points that share a
+      frequency but belong to different variants, since node names must be
+      unique. Which variant an entry applies to comes from opp-supported-hw.
+
+    properties:
+      opp-hz: true
+      opp-microvolt: true
+      opp-supported-hw: true
+
+    required:
+      - opp-hz
+
+dependencies:
+  "rockchip,grf": ["rockchip,volt-mem-read-margin"]
+  rockchip,volt-mem-read-margin: ["rockchip,grf"]
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    opp-table-npu {
+        compatible = "operating-points-v2-rknpu";
+
+        rockchip,grf = <&npu_grf>;
+        rockchip,volt-mem-read-margin = <855000 1>,
+                                        <765000 2>,
+                                        <675000 3>,
+                                        <495000 4>;
+
+        opp-300000000 {
+            opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <300000000>;
+            opp-microvolt = <750000>;
+            opp-supported-hw = <0xf9 0xffff>;
+        };
+
+        opp-300000000-1 {
+            opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <300000000>;
+            opp-microvolt = <750000>;
+            opp-supported-hw = <0x06 0xffff>;
+        };
+    };
